WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.280
"Medically Assisted Death"

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.920
There are limits

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.480
to palliative care.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:11.760
Even under hospice,

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.120
where one would assume
excellent palliative care,

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.440
there are those
who spend their last months

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.920
in uncontrolled pain.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.800
And, this unbearable suffering,

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.520
despite our best efforts,

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.560
leads to requests by patients

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.840
to end their life prematurely.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.000
Physician-assisted suicide,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.400
or perhaps more accurately

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.480
physician-assisted dying

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.640
or medical aid in dying,

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.040
allows the terminally ill
to end their lives

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.000
through the voluntary
self-administration

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.840
of a lethal dose of medication

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.560
expressly prescribed
by a physician for that purpose.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.480
U.S. public opinion has shifted

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.000
towards greater acceptance
of the process.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.960
By 2017, fully two-thirds
of U.S. adults

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.560
support legalizing the practice,

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:57.520
though in the same year,

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.840
dozens of states reviewed
and rejected legalization.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:02.800
A similar percentage

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.000
of terminally-ill patients
support it,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.520
though only about one in nine

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.240
then seriously considered
requesting it for themselves.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.480
Geriatrics physicians are split,

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.320
with 47 percent supporting

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:17.480
and 52 percent
opposing the practice.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.160
Of 150 professional
medical societies,

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.040
not a single one

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.720
has come out in favor
of medical aid in dying.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.040
Only 12 took
any sort of position,

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.640
mostly in opposition,

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.720
like the
American Medical Association,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.880
though some, including

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.800
the American Academy of Hospice
and Palliative Medicine,

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.880
took an official
neutral position.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.240
At the time I write this,

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.480
physician-assisted suicide
is only legal in nine states

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.320
plus the District of Columbia:

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:45.560
California,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.480
Colorado,

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:47.360
Hawaii,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.200
Maine,

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.240
Oregon,

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.200
Vermont,

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.600
and Washington,

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.080
plus New Jersey in 2019

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.640
and New Mexico in 2021.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.080
After, or pending legalization,

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.520
most of the affected
state medical societies

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.000
adopted a neutral position.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.600
Second only to Switzerland,

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.680
the first state
to legalize was Oregon,

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.840
with its Death With Dignity Act

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:16.560
passed
by ballot initiative in 1994

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.760
(though it didn't go into effect

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.720
until an injunction against it
was overturned in 1997).

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.160
It was upheld by the
U .S. Supreme Court in 2006,

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.400
after which other state bills
began to be introduced.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.560
In the few decades
since it's been active,

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.560
about 3,000
terminally-ill Oregonians

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.360
have received
such prescriptions,

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.400
though only about 2,000
decided to go through with it.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.880
(Nine patients regained
consciousness after ingestion.)

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.920
More recently,
that proportion has flipped,

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.920
with only about one-third
of those afforded the option

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.280
ended up using it
to end their lives,

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.760
supporting the premise that

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.240
much of the value to patients

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.160
may just lie
in having the choice.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.480
In Oregon,
the Death With Dignity Act

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:02.760
now accounts for about
one in 200 deaths in Oregon,

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.920
similar to physician assisted
suicide rates

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.000
in some European countries
that have legalized it.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.960
Medical aid
in dying is now legal

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.240
in Belgium, Luxembourg,

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.920
the Netherlands,
and Switzerland,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.520
along with Canada, Colombia,

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.040
and one state
in Australia (Victoria).

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.120
In some countries,

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.800
that aid is more direct
than others.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.160
In Belgium and the Netherlands,

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.000
euthanasia is legal,

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.440
where the physician can actively
administer the lethal medication

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.160
to someone seeking it
to end their life

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:33.200
due to unbearable,
incurable suffering.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.393
Death by euthanasia
now accounts for about

00:03:35.393 --> 00:03:39.360
one in 25 deaths
in those countries.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.160
Euthanasia is illegal
everywhere in the United States.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.080
In 40 states,
any physician aid in dying

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.600
is illegal
and punishable by law.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.080
In Montana,
the state supreme court

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.360
effectively decriminalized it,

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.520
and a 2021 bill to remove it
as a defense against

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.760
charging prescribing doctors
with homicide

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.800
failed in the Montana Senate
with a vote of 25 to 25.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.800
In contrast, V.S.E.D.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.600
is legal throughout the U.S.:

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:13.360
voluntarily stopping
eating and drinking,

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.120
which I detail
in a series of videos

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:29.600
starting with
How to Die a Good Death.

